			"Message": "fix(Project): Sync submodules with sidebar fix and extension scan improvements\n\nMulti-component synchronization addressing Activity Bar emptiness and extension loading:\n\n1. Mountain: Add Sky event replay on listener registration - Mountain emits events before Sky listeners install, causing dropped `sky://tree-view/create` and `sky://scm/register` events. New `sky:replay-events` handler iterates active TreeViews and SCM providers to re-emit. Also adds path security checks and SCM provider emit failure logging.\n\n2. Output: Add retry logic to user extension scan path - User extension paths lacked the retry logic that system paths had, causing silent 0-extension responses. Add exponential backoff (100-200-400-800-1500ms) for async disk scans.\n\n3. Sky: Fix Rollup no-external dropping VS Code contribution imports - Activity Bar came up empty because Rollup was dropping side-effect imports (`extensions.contribution`, `scm.contribution`, `files.contribution`, `*.viewlet.js`...). Add normalized path matching for disk paths, package specs, and lowercase variants.\n\n4. Cocoon: Refactor code structure for improved readability and maintainability.\n\nImpact: Activity Bar now populates with extension-contributed views (GitLens, jsdebug, SCM providers). User extensions load properly at boot even when Mountain's async scan hasn't completed.",
			"SHA": "972a110b4e940290d87a1a0af952d93f16b42318"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T02:13:47Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "fix(Project): Fix circuit breaker trips from URI parsing and service isolation\n\nMulti-component synchronization preventing silent error cascades:\n\n1. **Mountain**: Fix false circuit breaker trips from URI parsing edge cases - Extensions frequently register watchers on optional paths (e.g., `~/.roo/skills-*`, `.vscode/settings.json` in fresh workspaces) that don't exist. Mountain now catches benign \"path not found\" errors and records a deferred entry. Additionally, Cocoon sends URIs in three formats (plain strings, objects with `external` field, legacy `scheme`+`path` objects), but only the `external` field was accepted, causing `Diagnostic.Set` to trip the breaker after 5 publishes, silencing all linters.\n\n2. **Output**: Fix ExposeWorkbenchAccessor transform silently failing - The import marker used single quotes but esbuild rewrites to double quotes post-bundle, causing the entire `__CEL_SERVICES__` patch to no-op (all SkyBridge hooks offline). Also wraps each `invokeFunction` in its own try-IIFE so a single missing service doesn't throw the entire facade undefined.\n\nImpact: File watchers no longer fail on fresh workspaces. Language extension diagnostics now publish without triggering circuit breaker. All SkyBridge services (search, SCM, status bar, tree views) now initialize correctly.",
			"SHA": "7cc10566bad81808c5008aaa95a040fb6b3c133f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T01:40:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠇⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				2
			],
			"Message": "fix(Mountain): Accept numeric handles in FileWatcher and improve 404 detection\n\nSynchronize Mountain submodule with two bug fixes:\n\n1. **FileWatcher.rs**: Handle both numeric and string handle types in `RegisterWatcher` and `UnregisterWatcher`. The newer `NextProviderHandle()` returns a number, while older callers pass strings. Previously, numeric handles were silently converted to empty strings causing failures.\n\n2. **MountainVinegRPCService.rs**: Extend 404-like error detection to include `FileSystem.ReadDirectory` and additional error message patterns (\"no such file or directory\", \"entity not found\", \"os error 2\"). Return distinct error code `-32004` for benign 404s so Cocoon's shim can classify them without regex string parsing, while `-32000` remains the catch-all for genuine failures.\n\nImpact: File watcher registration now works correctly regardless of handle type. Directory listing 404s are properly distinguished from genuine errors, improving error handling accuracy in Cocoon.",
			"SHA": "563a19a149ccdbc2242f4f49537cad5d6200c86f"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-29T01:04:05Z",
			"File": [
				"⡟⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				4
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync submodules with worker bootstrap fix and dependency updates\n\nMulti-component synchronization bringing stability and dependency updates:\n\n1. **Output**: Add RewritePerfBaselineWorker transform to fix timer service worker bootstrap crashes. The transform removes `__name(...)` decoration from `(function() {...}).toString()` source that gets mangled by Vite when inlined into Astro chunks, causing `ReferenceError: Can't find variable: $4e` at runtime. Also fixes Tauri's `.env` overriding Build.sh's `NODE_ENV` by gating debug profiles on `Debug=true`.\n\n2. **Mountain**: Update build.rs comments to document PascalCase environment variable naming convention (`Profile`, `Pack`, `Bundle`, `Compiler`) introduced in the 2026-04-29 migration, replacing legacy `LAND_*` names.\n\n3. **Sky**: Bump Astro from 6.1.9 to 6.1.10 and remove unused empty `.env.example` template file.\n\n4. **Cocoon**: Sync to latest upstream extension host implementation.\n\nImpact: Timer service worker now boots correctly without mangled reference errors. Debug builds properly use readable output.",
			"SHA": "beecb3ff68cc233a0bb6c55a389cdd830e204917"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T23:06:46Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				28,
				5
			],
			"Message": "chore(Project): Sync submodules with diagnostics pipeline and service worker fix\n\nMulti-component synchronization enabling language extension diagnostics to render in the editor UI:\n\n1. **Mountain**: Extend DiagnosticsChanged event with per-URI marker payloads and cap keyring crate logging to Warn level. The new `changedURIs` field enables direct `IMarkerService.changeOne()` calls without extra IPC round-trips.\n\n2. **Output**: Add RewriteNodeModulesPath transform to fix hardcoded `vs/../../node_modules` paths that were causing grammar/tokenization to silently fail (returning SPA fallback). Also expose IMarkerService on `__CEL_SERVICES__.Markers` for SkyBridge to push diagnostics.\n\n3. **Sky**: Add `sky://diagnostics/changed` handler that translates Mountain events into editor markers. Receives `{ owner, changedURIs: [{ uri, markers }] }` and calls `Markers.changeOne()` for each entry - enabling red squiggles and Problems panel population.\n\n4. **Worker**: Remove obsolete precache paths from Service Worker that caused `Failed to fetch` errors on every install (paths moved to Astro chunks).\n\nImpact: Language extension compile errors, lint warnings, and type errors from extensions like rust-analyzer, TypeScript, and ESLint now render as visible markers in the editor.",
			"SHA": "7b62875b249ff5efc473887e164b325f25a135ff"
		}
	],
